35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The hours show chasing money takes six hours a month, which is too much.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The bank statements show a third of renewals only cleared after two rounds of reminders.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,The sign-up records show eleven people needed hand-worked part-year calculations to join.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,The weekday turnout fell by a third after the summer outings added a door charge.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The data confirms the core nine do the work while the rest barely show.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if reminders take so long, a single yearly payment would save that time.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"A single payment would help, but the ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,The taster forms show nine people refused a whole year at once.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,The winter social notes say the quieter members feel uneasy about what each outing costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"The ledger shows the core nine cover the fixed costs, so the rest are subsidizing them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I am worried that a yearly fee will scare off the people who only come sometimes.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The fixed costs mean we need a base fee that covers the hall and insurance.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,We need a way to let people join for a season without a full year.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,The hesitation is real; people are weighing up whether they belong enough to pay.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The core nine are carrying the load, so the fee should reflect that reality.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I think a base fee plus a small per-session charge might balance the books and the feelings.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,That structure would cover the fixed costs while keeping the variable costs visible.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,A seasonal option would let newcomers drift in without the pressure of a full year.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"If the per-session charge is small, it might remove the hesitation about committing to a whole year.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"The core nine will still pay the base fee, but the per-session charge will be fair to the rest.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
